# Chroma library, modern Earth: CLASH MOMENTS (v25 prep, Library, 10-23). Goes to chroma-library/earth_clash.lib.
# Syntax: header of build.py, plus the v25 keys clash:, band: (moment) and clash: (option), and the slots
# {clash.setting}, {clash.holder}, {clash.ally}, {clash.scene} (POUR-NOTES.md, "build.py support to add on Friday").
# Rule: chroma-ideas/life-drivers-2026-10-20/v25-specs.md, card 3; keys: chroma-engine/notes/v25/other-shapes.md, 3.
# Twelve templates: six settings x two bands. per_year is 0 everywhere: the Engine sends a clash when it applies.
# Balance layout: five one-colour options and one full cross cycle (s1 W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W, s2 W>B U>R B>G R>W G>U),
# six templates on each cycle. Each kind has one single and one cross. Every scene is a concrete demand with real
# stakes (an hour, a course, a rota, a vow, a closure, a vote), never "they are different", and never names the ways.
# The two give_in options are two of: willing agreement, strategic accommodation, constrained obedience (marked in
# the plan below as will, strat, con). Teen leaves are bounded and safe (a grandparent's, another school after a
# talk, a year out at 16+ with a parent's say, quitting a Saturday job or a club), and may only half work.
# Nothing here is built or run. Nothing reads this file until the Engine's clash switch is on, so no life changes.
#
# Plan: which colour takes which kind (single colour + cross), per template.
#
#   template              cycle  confront   give_in             leave      own_scene  bridge
#   household teen        s1     W + R>G    U strat + G>W will  B + W>U    R + U>B    G + B>R
#   household adult       s2     G + B>G    W will + R>W con    U + G>U    B + W>B    R + U>R
#   school teen           s2     R + U>R    G will + B>G strat  W + R>W    U + G>U    B + W>B
#   school adult          s1     B + W>U    R con + U>B strat   G + B>R    W + R>G    U + G>W
#   work teen             s1     U + G>W    B strat + W>U will  R + U>B    G + B>R    W + R>G
#   work adult            s2     W + R>W    U strat + G>U con   B + W>B    R + U>R    G + B>G
#   congregation teen     s2     G + B>G    W will + R>W con    U + G>U    B + W>B    R + U>R
#   congregation adult    s1     R + U>B    G will + B>R strat  W + R>G    U + G>W    B + W>U
#   town teen             s1     B + W>U    R con + U>B strat   G + B>R    W + R>G    U + G>W
#   town adult            s2     U + G>U    B strat + W>B con   R + U>R    G + B>G    W + R>W
#   group teen            s2     W + R>W    U strat + G>U will  B + W>B    R + U>R    G + B>G
#   group adult           s1     G + B>R    W will + R>G con    U + G>W    B + W>U    R + U>B
#
# Colour by kind over the twelve templates: singles + crosses led = total (each cell's ideal is 4.8).
#
#        confront    give_in     leave       own_scene   bridge
#   W    3 + 2 = 5   3 + 2 = 5   2 + 3 = 5   2 + 3 = 5   2 + 2 = 4
#   U    2 + 2 = 4   3 + 2 = 5   3 + 2 = 5   2 + 3 = 5   2 + 3 = 5
#   B    2 + 3 = 5   2 + 2 = 4   3 + 2 = 5   3 + 2 = 5   2 + 3 = 5
#   R    2 + 3 = 5   2 + 3 = 5   2 + 2 = 4   3 + 2 = 5   3 + 2 = 5
#   G    3 + 2 = 5   2 + 3 = 5   2 + 3 = 5   2 + 2 = 4   3 + 2 = 5
#
# As the second colour of a cross: W 3 3 2 1 3, U 3 3 3 2 1, B 1 3 3 3 2, R 2 1 3 3 3, G 3 2 1 3 3 (same column order).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- household, teen (cycle s1)

== the new rule at home
tier: life event
clash: household
band: teen
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 10-19
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: family, home
horizon: months
roles: parent, sibling, grandparent, friend
earth: a new rule at home, back by nine on school nights, and it falls on the one evening that matters
tribal: a new rule of the hearth, back inside the camp by dark, on the very nights that matter most to {N}
magic: a new rule of the house, doors barred at the ninth bell, on the one evening {N} lives for
scene: A new rule has come down from {clash.holder} for everyone in {clash.setting}: back by nine on school nights, and no arguing about it. The one evening of the week that matters most to {N} runs until ten. The whole house is waiting to see what {N} does.
scene tribal: The word from {clash.holder} has been said at the fire: back inside the camp by dark, every night, no exceptions. The gatherings {N} cares about begin after dark. The whole hearth is waiting to see what {N} does.
scene magic: The wards of {clash.setting} now close at the ninth bell, on the word of {clash.holder}. The one evening {N} lives for runs past the tenth. The household is waiting to see what {N} does.
- W | write down why the rule is unfair, and ask for a proper family vote | v: universalism, conformity | clash: confront | foot: lesson rules can be argued fairly | chance: 50
- U | keep to the rule until the end of term, noting how it goes | v: self-direction, security | clash: give_in | foot: door gave in to pressure | chance: 85
- B | make a deal to sleep at {grandparent}'s on the nights that matter | v: power, self-direction | clash: leave | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 55
- R | spend every free hour you do have with the crowd at {clash.scene} | v: stimulation, hedonism | clash: own_scene | foot: place gather.circle; person friend | chance: 75
- G | ask {clash.ally} to sit down one evening with them and {clash.holder} | v: benevolence, tradition | clash: bridge | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 60
- W>U | apply for the summer course that boards away from home, every form done right | v: conformity, achievement | clash: leave | foot: door left home | chance: 60
- U>B | find a club that meets before nine, and soon help run it | v: self-direction, power | clash: own_scene | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 70
- B>R | offer a trade: home early all week, for one late evening a week | v: power, stimulation | clash: bridge | foot: lesson a fair trade can settle things | chance: 55
- R>G | argue it out loud at dinner, with {sibling} on your side | v: stimulation, benevolence | clash: confront | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 45
- G>W | agree to the rule and mean it: the house runs better with it | v: benevolence, conformity | clash: give_in | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 90
works: The rule stays, but the one evening is allowed once a fortnight. Nobody quite won, and the house is calmer for it.
works: It takes a month of trying, and by the end of term the evening is {Ns} again, on conditions {N} did not choose.
fails: Nothing moves. The rule stands as it was, {N} misses the evening, and the house goes quiet in a cold way.
fails: It half works: the rule bends for two weeks, then snaps back the first time {N} is late.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- household, adult (cycle s2)

== the list on the kitchen wall
tier: life event
clash: household
band: adult
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: family, home, money
horizon: months
roles: parent, partner, sibling, friend
earth: a list on the kitchen wall says how the house is run now, and one line of it cuts across {Ns} plans
tribal: the elders of the hearth have shared out the winter's work and stores, and one share costs {N} dearly
magic: a sealed scroll of household rules hangs by the hearth, and one rule takes the very hours {N} planned for
scene: A list is pinned to the kitchen wall, in the hand of {clash.holder}: how {clash.setting} will be run from now on, who pays for what and who decides. Most of it is fair. One line, about {Ns} evenings and {Ns} share of the money, cuts straight across the life {N} has been building.
scene tribal: The elders of the hearth have shared out the winter's work and stores. Most of it is fair. The part that falls on {N} takes the days {N} had set aside for something of {Ns} own, and {clash.holder} will not hear a word against it.
scene magic: A new scroll of household rules hangs by the hearth, sealed by {clash.holder}. Most of it is fair. One rule, about who may use the house's study and when, takes the very hours {N} had planned for.
- W | agree to the list as written, and keep your part of it | v: conformity, security | clash: give_in | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 90
- U | move out to a place of your own, with the sums done first | v: self-direction, achievement | clash: leave | foot: mark left home | chance: 65
- B | spend your evenings with the people at {clash.scene}, who take your plans seriously | v: power, achievement | clash: own_scene | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 75
- R | cook a meal for the whole house, and say warmly what you need | v: stimulation, benevolence | clash: bridge | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 60
- G | remind {clash.holder} how this family always did it, and that it worked | v: tradition, benevolence | clash: confront | foot: lesson old ways can argue too | chance: 50
- W>B | join the residents' committee, where your way of running things is welcome | v: conformity, power | clash: own_scene | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 70
- U>R | write a new list with {clash.ally}, and bring it to the house together | v: self-direction, stimulation | clash: bridge | foot: person go-between | chance: 55
- B>G | say plainly that their own money stays their own unless that line changes | v: power, security | clash: confront | foot: person rival | chance: 45
- R>W | bite your tongue and keep to it, since the rent depends on it | v: security, conformity | clash: give_in | foot: mark gave in to pressure | chance: 90
- G>U | move back to the town you grew up in, and think it through there | v: tradition, self-direction | clash: leave | foot: mark moved away | chance: 60
works: The line is rewritten, not the way {N} wanted it, but in a way {N} can live with. The list stays on the wall.
works: {N} gets the evenings back, and pays for them with a bigger share of the chores.
fails: Nothing changes. The list stays as it is, and the kitchen is a tense place for a while.
fails: It half works: the money part is settled, and the evenings are argued over every week.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- school, teen (cycle s2)

== the subject that was taken off the timetable
tier: life event
clash: school
band: teen
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 11-19
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: school, family
horizon: months
roles: parent, sibling, friend, a teacher
earth: the new timetable puts {N} on the set course, and the subject {N} wanted most is gone from it
tribal: the elders have given out the crafts for the year, and {N} is set to learn the wrong one
magic: the masters have set the year's course of study, and the art {N} hoped to learn is not on it
scene: The new timetable is up at {clash.setting}, and {N} has been put on the set course. The subject {N} wanted most is gone from it, and {clash.holder} says there will be no changes this year. A whole year of {Ns} life has just been decided.
scene tribal: The elders have given out the crafts for the year, and {N} has been set to learn the one the family always learns. The craft {N} wanted goes to someone else, and {clash.holder} says it is settled.
scene magic: The masters of {clash.setting} have set the year's course of study. The art {N} hoped to learn is not on it, and {clash.holder} says the course is the same for every student.
- W | ask through the proper channels to move to the school that teaches it | v: conformity, achievement | clash: leave | foot: means ties-.03 | chance: 55
- U | teach yourself the subject at the library, with others who want it too | v: self-direction, achievement | clash: own_scene | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 75
- B | offer a deal: top marks on the set course, for one class of your choosing | v: achievement, power | clash: bridge | foot: door kept your word | chance: 50
- R | stand up in assembly and say the timetable is wrong | v: stimulation, self-direction | clash: confront | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 40
- G | take the set course as {sibling} did, and give it a fair chance | v: tradition, security | clash: give_in | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 90
- W>B | ask {clash.ally} to put your case to {clash.holder}, with your marks to back it | v: conformity, achievement | clash: bridge | foot: person mentor | chance: 55
- U>R | bring the numbers: how many asked for the subject, and why it matters | v: self-direction, stimulation | clash: confront | foot: lesson facts carry weight sometimes | chance: 50
- B>G | take the set course for now, and plan the switch for next year | v: achievement, security | clash: give_in | foot: door gave in to pressure | chance: 85
- R>W | ask {parent} for a year out at sixteen, to work out what you want | v: stimulation, conformity | clash: leave | foot: means freedom+.06 | chance: 50
- G>U | join the after-school nature group, where your questions are welcome | v: benevolence, self-direction | clash: own_scene | foot: place gather.circle; person friend | chance: 75
works: The subject comes back, as one lesson a week after school. It is not what {N} wanted, and it is something.
works: {N} gets the change, a term late and with a pile of catching up to do.
fails: The timetable stays as it is, and {N} spends the year on a course {N} did not choose.
fails: It half works: {clash.holder} agrees to look again next year, and this year is gone.

