== the course that wants it done one way
tier: life event
clash: school
band: adult
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-75
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: learning, work, money
horizon: months
roles: a teacher, friend, colleague, partner
earth: the college course marks every piece of work by the one approved method, and {Ns} own way fails
tribal: the old teacher of the craft will pass it on only if every step is done exactly the old way
magic: the college of mages grades every working by the approved method, and {Ns} own method fails
scene: At {clash.setting}, {clash.holder} has made it plain: every piece of work is done the one approved way and handed in on the set night, or it fails. {N} has another way that works, and a job and a life around the classes. The fees are already paid.
scene tribal: The old teacher of the craft has said it twice now: every step the old way, in the old order, or not at all. {N} has found a way that works better, and the teaching is the only way into the craft.
scene magic: At {clash.setting}, {clash.holder} grades every working by the approved method and no other. {Ns} own method works, and fails the mark every time. The year's fees are paid.
- W | join the students' society, and help set its rules | v: conformity, universalism | clash: own_scene | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 75
- U | show {clash.holder} your method beside theirs, and ask for a fair trial | v: self-direction, achievement | clash: bridge | foot: person teacher | chance: 50
- B | tell {clash.holder} straight: mark the work on results, or lose a paying student | v: power, achievement | clash: confront | foot: person rival | chance: 45
- R | grit your teeth and do it their way, because the fees are spent | v: self-direction, security | clash: give_in | foot: mark gave in to pressure | chance: 85
- G | drop the course, and give the evenings back to the people at home | v: tradition, benevolence | clash: leave | foot: means time+.06 | chance: 75
- W>U | read the course rules closely, and appeal the marks by the book | v: conformity, self-direction | clash: confront | foot: lesson the small print cuts both ways | chance: 55
- U>B | do it their way to the letter, and keep your own method for later | v: achievement, power | clash: give_in | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 85
- B>R | walk out mid-term and put the time into a project of your own | v: power, stimulation | clash: leave | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 65
- R>G | find the crowd at {clash.scene} who learn by doing and argue till late | v: stimulation, benevolence | clash: own_scene | foot: place gather.circle; person friend | chance: 70
- G>W | ask {clash.ally}, who knows both sides, to find a way through for everyone | v: benevolence, conformity | clash: bridge | foot: person go-between | chance: 60
works: One piece of work done {Ns} way is allowed, as a trial. It passes, narrowly, and the rule bends a little.
works: {N} gets through the course, with a certificate and a few scars from the argument.
fails: The rule holds, and {Ns} best piece of work comes back marked as a fail.
fails: It half works: one mark is changed on appeal, and the rest of the year is done the approved way.

