earth: the new rota at the Saturday job takes every weekend, and an unpaid half hour to close up
tribal: the herder wants {N} with the flock every rest day now, as well as the working days
magic: the workshop's master wants {N} at the bench every free day, and sweeping up after closing too
scene: The new rota is up at {clash.setting}: {N} now works every Saturday and most Sundays, and stays on unpaid to close up. That is how it works now, says {clash.holder}: take it or leave it. The money matters, and so does everything else {N} used to do with the weekend.
scene tribal: The herder has told {N} to come with the flock every rest day as well as the working days. The share of the herd is good. The rest days were the only days {N} had for anything else.
scene magic: The master of {clash.setting} wants {N} at the bench every free day now, and sweeping the floor after closing for nothing. The coin is welcome, and the free days were everything else.
- W | ask {clash.ally} to help draw up a fair rota that everyone signs | v: universalism, conformity | clash: bridge | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 60
- U | bring {clash.holder} the hours, written down, and the rules on young workers | v: self-direction, achievement | clash: confront | foot: lesson knowing the rules helps | chance: 55
- B | take the extra hours for now, and save the money for something better | v: achievement, security | clash: give_in | foot: means money+.06 | chance: 85
- R | quit on the spot, and take your weekends back | v: stimulation, hedonism | clash: leave | foot: means freedom+.06 | chance: 70
- G | find weekend work at the farm shop, where the regulars know your name | v: benevolence, security | clash: own_scene | foot: place prod.land | chance: 65
- W>U | agree to the rota and learn the work properly, start to finish | v: conformity, achievement | clash: give_in | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 85
- U>B | line up a better job first, then hand in your notice | v: achievement, power | clash: leave | foot: person boss | chance: 55
- B>R | start selling what you make at the weekend market, on your own terms | v: power, stimulation | clash: own_scene | foot: place comm.market | chance: 60
- R>G | get the whole crew together and ask {clash.holder}, cheerfully, for a fairer rota | v: stimulation, benevolence | clash: bridge | foot: person colleague | chance: 55
- G>W | speak up for all the young ones on the rota, not just yourself | v: benevolence, universalism | clash: confront | foot: person rival | chance: 45
works: The Sundays go back to how they were, and the closing half hour is paid. The Saturdays stay.
works: {N} keeps one free weekend a month, and the pay goes down a little to match.
fails: The rota stays as it is, take it or leave it, and {N} is a little less welcome at work.
fails: It half works: the unpaid half hour stops, and every weekend is still taken.

