- U>R | join the trade's evening meetups, where people swap better ways of doing it | v: self-direction, stimulation | clash: own_scene | foot: place gather.talk | chance: 75
- B>G | propose a trial: your team works your way for a month, results on the table | v: achievement, security | clash: bridge | foot: lesson results speak for themselves | chance: 50
- R>W | tell {clash.holder}, in front of everyone, that this will wreck the work | v: stimulation, universalism | clash: confront | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 40
- G>U | keep your head down and do it their way: people at home rely on the wage | v: benevolence, security | clash: give_in | foot: mark gave in to pressure | chance: 90
works: The new way stays, with one exception carved out for the part {N} does best. {N} still hates the board.
works: {N} lands on their feet, a few months poorer in patience, and the work is good again.
fails: Nothing bends. The targets go up on the board, and {Ns} name is near the bottom of it.
fails: It half works: {clash.holder} listens, nods, and changes the hours but not the rest.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- congregation, teen (cycle s2)

== the promises at the coming of age
tier: life event
clash: congregation
band: teen
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 11-19
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: faith, family
horizon: months
roles: parent, grandparent, friend, elder
earth: {N} is to stand up at the coming-of-age gathering and say the promises, and is not sure they are true for {N}
tribal: the elders expect {N} at the coming-of-age rite, to speak the old vows in front of the whole clan
magic: the temple expects {N} to take the novice's vows at the turning of the year, before the whole house
scene: Next month {N} is to stand up at {clash.setting} and say the promises of the coming of age, in front of everyone. The family expects it, and so does {clash.holder}. {N} is not sure the words are true for {N}, and saying them would mean something.
scene tribal: At the next full moon {N} is to stand before the whole clan and speak the old vows. The family's place in the clan rests on it, and {clash.holder} expects it. {N} is not sure the vows are {Ns} own.
scene magic: At the turning of the year {N} is to take the novice's vows before the whole house. {Ns} name is already written in the book, in the hand of {clash.holder}. {N} is not sure the vows are {Ns} to make.
- W | stand up and say the promises: the family has done it for generations | v: tradition, conformity | clash: give_in | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 90
- U | ask {parent} for a year's wait, to decide when older | v: self-direction, security | clash: leave | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 55
- B | find the young people's group that debates the big questions, and soon lead it | v: power, achievement | clash: own_scene | foot: place faith.seeking | chance: 70
- R | tell {clash.ally} how you feel, all of it, and ask for help | v: stimulation, benevolence | clash: bridge | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 65
- G | tell {clash.holder} the old words deserve someone who means them | v: tradition, universalism | clash: confront | foot: lesson doubt can be said kindly | chance: 50
- W>B | join the volunteers who visit the care home, and serve without the vows | v: conformity, achievement | clash: own_scene | foot: place care.houses | chance: 75
- U>R | ask {clash.holder} the questions you really have, and see if there is room | v: self-direction, stimulation | clash: bridge | foot: person mentor | chance: 50
- B>G | say you will stand up only if you may say the words your own way | v: power, tradition | clash: confront | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 40
- R>W | say the words for the family's sake, though your heart is not in it | v: security, conformity | clash: give_in | foot: mark gave in to pressure | chance: 90
- G>U | spend the summer at {grandparent}'s, away from it all, to think it through | v: tradition, self-direction | clash: leave | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 60
works: The day is put off a year, with the family's grudging blessing, and {N} has time to find out what {N} thinks.
works: {N} stands up and says the promises in words that are partly {Ns} own, and nobody objects.
fails: The day comes as planned. {N} goes through with it, and the doubt is still there afterwards.
fails: It half works: {clash.holder} agrees to wait, and the family talks of little else all summer.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- congregation, adult (cycle s1)

== what the congregation now expects
tier: life event
clash: congregation
band: adult
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: faith, community, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, partner, elder, neighbour
earth: two evenings a week for the congregation's work, every gathering, and no open disagreement with its decisions
tribal: the keeper of the sacred fire asks more of everyone now, and wants no voice raised against the old ruling
magic: the temple's high keeper demands more service of every member, and silence about its rulings
scene: The word from {clash.holder} to {clash.setting} is plain: from now on, every member at every gathering, two evenings a week for the congregation's work, and no open disagreement with its decisions. {N} has a family, a job and opinions, and {Ns} friends of twenty years are all here.
scene tribal: The keeper of the sacred fire has asked more of everyone: a night a week at the fire, a share of every hunt, and no voice raised against the old ruling. {N} has a family to feed and a view of the ruling, and every friend {N} has sits at that fire.
scene magic: The high keeper of {clash.setting} has demanded more service of every member, and silence about the temple's rulings. {N} has work, a family and doubts about one ruling in particular, and the temple is where {Ns} oldest friends are.
